:{"code":"/-- The `i + j`-th element of a list coincides with the `j`-th element of the list obtained by\ndropping the first `i` elements. Version designed to rewrite from the small list to the big list. -/\n@[simp, grind =] theorem getElem_drop {xs : List α} {i : Nat} {j : Nat} {h : j < (xs.drop i).length} :\n    (xs.drop i)[j] = xs[i + j]'(by\n      rw [Nat.add_comm]\n      exact Nat.add_lt_of_lt_sub (length_drop ▸ h)) := by\n  rw [getElem_drop']","start":232,"end":238},"axioms":["propext"]}